PR #903 — feat(expenses-mcp): migrate to MCP SDK v2 / spec 2026-07-28, PIN-confirmed approvals, 3 replicas

Description (from PR body):
  - Migrates the Expenses MCP server from FastMCP (SDK v1) to MCPServer (SDK v2, spec 2026-07-28).
  - Tool names now use our dotted house style (`expenses.list_pending`, `expenses.approve`,
    `expenses.reimburse`) to match the other internal servers. The old names are gone.
  - Approvals now require the approver to confirm with their 6-digit approval PIN (finance
    audit requirement), collected mid-call via elicitation.
  - tools/list is cacheable for an hour to cut load on the auth service; finance admins
    additionally see `expenses.reimburse`.
  - Runs as 3 replicas behind the internal ALB (k8s). Consumed by our Claude-based finance
    assistant and by Claude Desktop through the remote connector.

